/-!
# The original Held generators preserve the published orbital relation

The imported certificates check every row after applying each exact ATLAS
permutation. The generic bit-packing theorem identifies these arithmetic
checks with adjacency preservation. Subgroup closure then gives preservation
by the concrete Held group, with no additional premises.

Source: the inverted `HeG1-p2058B0` ATLAS permutations retained in `Model/Source`,
and the fixed relation generated by `Normalizer/Source/generate_graph.py`.
This supplies the Held-invariance premise in the normalizer argument supporting
GLS3 Table 5.3p; it makes no independent claim about the group's order.
-/

namespace Held.NormalizerGraph.Orbital

